cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "pitchcropper: automated pitch boundary and camera crop engine"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Anowar Hossen Farvez
    given-names: Anowar
    email: "farvez.capt@gmail.com"
repository-code: "https://github.com/capt-farvez/pitchcropper"
license: MIT
date-released: "2026-09-29"
version: "0.1.0"
abstract: >-
  A batch pipeline that detects the playing-field boundary in a sampled set of
  frames from match video, aggregates the valid detections into one result,
  and reports progress and outcome to a platform API. Built from a research
  prototype for a backend developer assessment; all data is synthetic.
